### 3.2 Fragmentation

Once the hard scattering has taken place the scattered partons will fragment into further partons and finally hadronise to form colour neutral hadrons. There are currently three leading theories regarding hadronisation, the string model [53], the independent fragmentation model [54] and the cluster model [55], which has been subject to recent modification [56].

The string model uses gluons as field lines, utilising the self-interaction of gluons to justify com

