### 6.3 Identified Hadron Ratios From Unidentified Neutral Energy Triggered \(\Delta\phi\) Correlations

The \(\frac{dE}{dx}\) data from the correlations in the previous section were analysed using the calibrated Bichsel functions for charged pions, kaons, electrons and protons. Positive and negative hadrons were combined to maximise the statistics that had been reduced having separated the data into three regions.

